t cecil rhodes i'm not amazed  that you know people of color and black  and minority ethnic histories are  emitted  from the british curriculum but what i  think is more important is that other  people who are non-black and minority  ethnic  need to be amazed across the country  last night  people took a knee in solidarity with  the black lives matter movement  campaigners say making black history  part of the national curriculum  will be an even more powerful long-term  message  and the brady sky news in oxford
 

